<title>JAPAN: NEC boosts notebook PC output by 25 pct.</title>
<headline>NEC boosts notebook PC output by 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>NEC Corp said on Monday it had boosted production of notebook personal computers (PCs) at a subsidiary to 100,000 units per month, up 25 percent from a year ago.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the increase was achieved through improved production efficiency and did not involve a major investment in new equipment.</p>
<p>The company's notebook PCs are produced by its subsidiary NEC Yonezawa Ltd.</p>
